---
// Frames attach to a fleet through HQ. The same frames, the same hives, and
// the two HQ configuration carriers a fleet can select: hq.mode: git (the
// shipped default) and hq.mode: dolt-server (a proposed binding, implemented
// behind a selector; no cutover recorded). Source: docs/HQ.md,
// docs/FRAME-FLEET-MEMBERSHIP.md, docs/design/frame-dolt-server-hq-mode-adr.md,
// docs/HUB.md. HQ's own beads and the per-host hub are drawn because they are
// what does NOT change between the modes.
---
<figure id="fig-frames-hq">
  <div class="diagram">
    <svg viewBox="0 0 1160 600" role="img"
      aria-label="Topology diagram. Top row: two active frames each holding one hive's lease, a drained standby frame, and a laptop in viewer role; each frame signs with its own SSH key and keeps a derived per-host hub. Middle: the hive repositories whose git remotes carry branches and refs/dolt/data. Bottom: two HQ configuration modes side by side. Git mode, shipped default: an HQ git repository holding fleet.yaml, workspace.toml and host manifests on main and HQ beads on refs/dolt/data; frames clone it and publish signed heartbeats and leases through git. Dolt-server mode, proposed: a central Dolt SQL server with a committed configuration snapshot and live lease and report tables that are never committed; frames connect with per-incarnation SQL principals and signed envelopes, a trusted observer verifies, and an outage fails closed with no fallback to git. HQ beads stay on their own Dolt replication in both modes.">
      <defs>
        <marker id="fh-n" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="6" markerHeight="6" orient="auto-start-reverse">
          <path d="M0,0 L10,5 L0,10 z" fill="var(--ink-3)"/></marker>
        <marker id="fh-h" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="6" markerHeight="6" orient="auto-start-reverse">
          <path d="M0,0 L10,5 L0,10 z" fill="var(--honey)"/></marker>
      </defs>

      <!-- ===== frames ===== -->
      <text class="d-kicker" x="24" y="28">FRAMES — ONE PRIMARY HOST PER HIVE · SIGNED HEARTBEATS · ELIGIBILITY RE-CHECKED AT EVERY CLAIM</text>
      {[
        { x: 24,  cls: 'd-box-g', name: 'frame-builder-01', state: 'active · executor', lease: 'lease: github/acme/api', note: 'runs seats for api' },
        { x: 306, cls: 'd-box-g', name: 'frame-builder-02', state: 'active · executor', lease: 'lease: github/acme/web', note: 'runs seats for web' },
        { x: 588, cls: 'd-box-dir', name: 'frame-builder-03', state: 'drained · standby', lease: 'attached to api, no lease', note: 'failover, not parallel capacity' },
        { x: 870, cls: 'd-chip', name: 'laptop', state: 'viewer', lease: 'no lease — reads and files', note: 'bh hub bd ready · bh report' },
      ].map((f) => (
        <g>
          <rect class={f.cls} x={f.x} y="40" width="266" height="96" rx="8"/>
          <text class="d-title" x={f.x + 14} y="62">{f.name}</text>
          <text class="d-code-h" x={f.x + 14} y="78">{f.state}</text>
          <text class="d-mute" x={f.x + 14} y="94">{f.lease}</text>
          <text class="d-mute" x={f.x + 14} y="108">{f.note}</text>
          <text class="d-mute" x={f.x + 14} y="126">own SSH key · own derived hub</text>
        </g>
      ))}

      <!-- ===== hives ===== -->
      <line class="d-sep" x1="24" y1="152" x2="1136" y2="152"/>
      <text class="d-kicker" x="24" y="176">HIVE REPOS — EACH ON ITS OWN GIT REMOTE</text>
      {[
        { x: 24,  name: 'github/acme/api', },
        { x: 306, name: 'github/acme/web', },
      ].map((h) => (
        <g>
          <rect class="d-chip" x={h.x} y="186" width="266" height="40" rx="6"/>
          <text class="d-code" x={h.x + 14} y="203">{h.name}</text>
          <text class="d-mute" x={h.x + 14} y="218">branches · refs/dolt/data · nothing hosted</text>
        </g>
      ))}
      <path class="flow" d="M 157 136 V 182" marker-end="url(#fh-n)"/>
      <path class="flow" d="M 439 136 V 182" marker-end="url(#fh-n)"/>
      <text class="d-mute" x="600" y="203">a frame pushes wt/ branches and refs/dolt/data for the hive it leases;</text>
      <text class="d-mute" x="600" y="218">bh sync hydrates every registered hive into each host's disposable hub (read side)</text>

      <!-- ===== HQ modes ===== -->
      <line class="d-sep" x1="24" y1="244" x2="1136" y2="244"/>
      <text class="d-kicker" x="470" y="268">HQ — hq.mode SELECTS THE CONFIG CARRIER</text>

      <!-- git mode -->
      <rect class="lane-i" x="24" y="280" width="548" height="304" rx="10"/>
      <text class="lane-label" x="40" y="302">hq.mode: git — shipped default</text>
      <rect class="d-box" x="40" y="316" width="516" height="118" rx="8"/>
      <text class="d-title" x="54" y="336">HQ repository · &lt;owner&gt;/beadhive-hq</text>
      <text class="d-code" x="54" y="354">main</text>
      <text class="d-mute" x="100" y="354">fleet.yaml (signed config carrier v2) · workspace.toml · hosts/&lt;host&gt;.yaml</text>
      <text class="d-code" x="54" y="372">refs/dolt/data</text>
      <text class="d-mute" x="150" y="372">HQ-origin beads (hq- prefix): escalations, leases, policy</text>
      <text class="d-mute" x="54" y="392">frames: bh hq clone → read fleet config · publish manifests, heartbeats and</text>
      <text class="d-mute" x="54" y="406">lease CAS as signed commits · director / custodian write via bh hq push</text>
      <text class="d-mute" x="54" y="424">bh hq push never force-pushes; a three-level backup precedes the first wire</text>

      <path class="flow-h" d="M 157 226 V 312" marker-end="url(#fh-h)"/>
      <path class="flow-h" d="M 439 226 V 312" marker-end="url(#fh-h)"/>
      <text class="d-mute" x="166" y="252" style="font-size:9.5px">clone · push</text>

      <rect class="d-chip" x="40" y="446" width="250" height="124" rx="8"/>
      <text class="d-title" x="54" y="466">lease</text>
      <text class="d-mute" x="54" y="482">one primary executor per hive,</text>
      <text class="d-mute" x="54" y="496">compare-and-swap in HQ; viewers</text>
      <text class="d-mute" x="54" y="510">never claim. A second host waits</text>
      <text class="d-mute" x="54" y="524">out the TTL or adopts explicitly.</text>
      <text class="d-code" x="54" y="546">bh host lease adopt | release</text>
      <text class="d-code" x="54" y="560">bh host list --lease-hive &lt;hive&gt;</text>

      <rect class="d-chip" x="306" y="446" width="250" height="124" rx="8"/>
      <text class="d-title" x="320" y="466">heartbeat → admission</text>
      <text class="d-mute" x="320" y="482">signed, bounded record: frame id,</text>
      <text class="d-mute" x="320" y="496">host incarnation, key fingerprint,</text>
      <text class="d-mute" x="320" y="510">sequence, release, capacity.</text>
      <text class="d-mute" x="320" y="524">TTL exclusive, ≤ 900 s; three fresh</text>
      <text class="d-mute" x="320" y="538">beats before an operator may admit.</text>
      <text class="d-code" x="320" y="560">bh host admit plan | apply | check</text>

      <!-- dolt-server mode -->
      <rect class="d-box-dir" x="588" y="280" width="548" height="304" rx="10"/>
      <text class="lane-label" x="604" y="302">hq.mode: dolt-server — proposed binding</text>
      <rect class="d-chip-dir" x="1010" y="290" width="112" height="16" rx="8"/>
      <text class="d-mute" x="1066" y="302" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:9.5px">no cutover recorded</text>

      <rect class="d-box" x="604" y="316" width="516" height="118" rx="8"/>
      <text class="d-title" x="618" y="336">central Dolt SQL server · one database for membership</text>
      <text class="d-code" x="618" y="354">config tables</text>
      <text class="d-mute" x="716" y="354">committed snapshot, one publisher, explicit authoritative revision</text>
      <text class="d-code" x="618" y="372">frame_leases · frame_reports</text>
      <text class="d-mute" x="820" y="372">live working set · dolt_ignore · never committed</text>
      <text class="d-mute" x="618" y="392">frames: per-incarnation SQL principal, table grants only — SQL auth never makes</text>
      <text class="d-mute" x="618" y="406">a lease authoritative; every envelope still carries the frame's SSH signature</text>
      <text class="d-mute" x="618" y="424">trusted observer verifies signatures and replay receipts before anything counts</text>

      <path class="flow-h dashed" d="M 721 136 C 721 200, 760 250, 790 312" marker-end="url(#fh-h)"/>
      <text class="d-mute" x="800" y="252" style="font-size:9.5px">SQL + signed envelopes · no HQ checkout</text>

      <rect class="d-chip" x="604" y="446" width="250" height="124" rx="8"/>
      <text class="d-title" x="618" y="466">readiness is three checks</text>
      <text class="d-code-g" x="618" y="484">CONFIG_READY</text><text class="d-mute" x="716" y="484">revision + HQ identity</text>
      <text class="d-code-g" x="618" y="500">BEADS_READY</text><text class="d-mute" x="716" y="500">store or recoverable origin</text>
      <text class="d-code-g" x="618" y="516">AUTHORITY_READY</text><text class="d-mute" x="736" y="516">signed authority verifies</text>
      <text class="d-mute" x="618" y="538">then ADMITTED by an operator, then</text>
      <text class="d-mute" x="618" y="552">ELIGIBLE per hive. One true, others</text>
      <text class="d-mute" x="618" y="566">false, is a normal state.</text>

      <rect class="d-box-r" x="870" y="446" width="250" height="124" rx="8"/>
      <text class="d-title" x="884" y="466">fails closed</text>
      <text class="d-mute" x="884" y="482">a configured SQL failure is</text>
      <text class="d-mute" x="884" y="496">unavailable: new intake denied,</text>
      <text class="d-mute" x="884" y="510">no fallback to git, no stale</text>
      <text class="d-mute" x="884" y="524">cached authority. Incumbent</text>
      <text class="d-mute" x="884" y="538">leases keep renewing under the</text>
      <text class="d-mute" x="884" y="552">original CAS and expiry rules.</text>

      <!-- what does not change -->
      <text class="d-mute" x="580" y="596" text-anchor="middle">In both modes HQ's own beads replicate as one Dolt database on one remote path, and every host rebuilds its hub locally — neither moves when the config carrier does.</text>
    </svg>
  </div>
  <div class="legend display">
    <span><span class="sw" style="background:var(--honey)"></span>frame ↔ HQ</span>
    <span><span class="sw" style="background:var(--ink-3)"></span>frame ↔ hive remote</span>
    <span><span class="sw dash"></span>proposed / standby</span>
  </div>
  <figcaption>Three stores, three jobs, and only one of them changes shape with
  <code>hq.mode</code>. Each <b>hive</b> keeps its issue history on its own remote; each host keeps a
  disposable <b>hub</b> it rebuilds with <code>bh sync</code>; <b>HQ</b> alone is authoritative for
  fleet membership, leases and HQ-origin beads. In <b>git mode</b> the fleet configuration travels
  as signed commits in an HQ repository every frame clones. In <b>dolt-server mode</b> the same
  configuration is a committed snapshot in a central SQL store, the live lease and heartbeat tables
  are deliberately never committed, and a frame needs no HQ checkout at all — but SQL credentials
  are never trusted on their own: the frame's SSH signature on every envelope is what makes a lease
  or heartbeat count, exactly as in git mode. A drained frame attached to a leased hive is standby
  for failover, not a second worker on the same hive.</figcaption>
</figure>
